{
  "code": "NJ",
  "name": "New Jersey",
  "year": 2026,
  "method": "bracket_per_period_rate_table",
  "$scopeNote": "STATE income tax (NJ-WT's five Rate Tables A-E) + UI/Workforce/Supplemental-Workforce employee contribution + Temporary Disability Insurance (TDI) employee contribution + Family Leave Insurance (FLI) employee contribution. New Jersey has NO local/municipal income tax anywhere in the state (unlike PA/OH/IN/KY in this project) -- confirmed by absence in NJ-WT, which covers only state-level withholding. Newark's well-known payroll tax is an EMPLOYER excise tax on payroll expense (1% of payroll over a threshold), not an employee withholding -- out of scope for this engine, same category as every other employer-side tax already excluded (federal FUTA aside, which the engine does model). Weekly/biweekly/semimonthly/monthly/annual periods only -- see knownGaps for quarterly/semiannual/daily.",
  "$methodComment": "NJ-WT's own 'Tables for Percentage Method of Withholding' (effective since Oct 1, 2020 -- the document fetched directly states this on its own cover page, and has not been revised since; NJ's GIT rate schedule itself hasn't changed since the 2020 'millionaire's tax' law). Mechanically closest to New York's bracket_per_period_net (subtract an allowance from PER-PERIOD gross wages, no annualizing, then look up the result in a table published separately per pay frequency) but with two genuine differences: (1) the allowance is a flat per-exemption dollar amount x count (NJ-WT's own worked instructions), not NY's precomputed combined-allowance table; (2) which of the five bracket schedules (Rate A/B/C/D/E) applies is a direct Form NJ-W4 election (Line 2 filing-status boxes, or an explicit Line 3 override) rather than a marital-status computation. See resolveNJRateTable() in src/taxes/state.ts. A genuine, independently-confirmed oddity carried over from NY's file: NJ's OWN withholding brackets top out at 11.8% (all five tables), a full percentage point above the actual GIT statutory top marginal rate of 10.75% for income over $1,000,000 -- this is NJ deliberately over-withholding high earners as a backstop against underpayment, not a transcription error (the top bracket is 11.8% identically across all five independently-transcribed tables, and NJ Div. of Taxation guidance elsewhere confirms 10.75% as the actual liability rate for that bracket).",
  "$extractionNote": "NJ-WT's own PDF text-extracts with the SAME multi-column layout hazard already documented for NY (pdftotext -layout interleaves adjacent tables' rows). Resolved differently than NY's fix (which switched to non-layout extraction): here, every table's ANNUAL boundaries+rates extracted cleanly (round numbers, no column collision), so each of Rate A-E's five sub-annual bracket schedules (weekly/biweekly/semimonthly/monthly) was DERIVED from the clean annual figures -- period boundary = round(annualBoundary / periodsPerYear), period base = round(annualBase / periodsPerYear, 2) -- rather than trusting the garbled per-period text directly. Verified exhaustively: recomputing this way reproduces literally every one of NJ-WT's own published weekly and monthly base figures to the cent (cross-checked for all five tables, e.g. Rate A weekly's $5.77/$11.54/$15.29/$56.35/$628.46/$1,580.38 bracket bases, Rate D weekly's $16.15, Rate E monthly's $50.01/$364.13/$2,530.84/$6,655.78 -- all exact matches), which also confirms the derivation method itself, not just these specific numbers.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "NJ-WT, New Jersey Income Tax Withholding Instructions (September 2025, covers 2026)",
      "url": "https://www.nj.gov/treasury/taxation/pdf/current/njwt.pdf",
      "verifiedOn": "2026-08-16",
      "verifiedBy": "Downloaded and text-extracted directly (pdftotext). Provided the \"Which Rate Table to Use\" instructions, the Withholding Allowance Value Table, and the supplemental-wages aggregation rule."
    },
    {
      "title": "New Jersey Withholding Rate Tables (Percentage Method, effective Oct 1, 2020)",
      "url": "https://www.nj.gov/treasury/taxation/pdf/withholdingtables.pdf",
      "verifiedOn": "2026-08-16",
      "verifiedBy": "Downloaded and text-extracted directly (pdftotext -layout). Source of Rate Tables A-E -- see $extractionNote above for how the per-period figures were reconstructed from this table's own annual figures."
    },
    {
      "title": "NJ Division of Employer Accounts — 2026 employee UI / Workforce Development / Supplemental Workforce Fund rates",
      "url": "https://www.nj.gov/labor/ea/employer-services/rate-info/",
      "verifiedOn": "2026-08-16",
      "verifiedBy": "Fetched directly. States the 2026 worker rate as 0.003825 (UI) and 0.000425 (WF/SWF) for January 1 - December 31, 2026; combined 0.425%, matching the $190.40 maximum annual employee withholding independently published in the NJDOL 2026 benefit-rates press release below ($44,800 wage base x 0.425% = $190.40, confirmed by direct calculation)."
    },
    {
      "title": "NJ Division of Temporary Disability and Family Leave Insurance — Worker TDI contribution rate",
      "url": "https://www.nj.gov/labor/myleavebenefits/worker/tdi/",
      "verifiedOn": "2026-08-16",
      "verifiedBy": "Fetched directly. Verbatim: \"workers contribute 0.19% on the first $171,100 (wage cap) in covered wages earned during this calendar year. The maximum worker contribution for 2026 is $325.09.\" Confirmed by calculation: $171,100 x 0.19% = $325.09."
    },
    {
      "title": "NJ Division of Temporary Disability and Family Leave Insurance — Worker FLI contribution rate",
      "url": "https://www.nj.gov/labor/myleavebenefits/worker/fli/",
      "verifiedOn": "2026-08-16",
      "verifiedBy": "Fetched directly. Verbatim: \"workers contribute 0.23% on the first $171,100 (wage cap) in covered wages earned during this calendar year. The maximum worker contribution for 2026 is $393.53.\" Confirmed by calculation: $171,100 x 0.23% = $393.53."
    },
    {
      "title": "NJDOL — New Benefit Rates for 2026 (taxable wage bases)",
      "url": "https://www.nj.gov/labor/lwdhome/press/2025/20251229_newbenefitrates2026.shtml",
      "verifiedOn": "2026-08-16",
      "verifiedBy": "Fetched directly. Confirms the UI taxable wage base ($44,800, up from $43,300) and the TDI/FLI taxable wage base ($171,100, up from $165,400) for 2026."
    }
  ],
