    "wageBase": 171100,
    "$comment": "Family Leave Insurance (FLI). Shares the same $171,100 TDI/FLI wage base, tracked separately per input.ytd.statePaidLeave.NJ."
  },
  "knownGaps": [
    "Quarterly, semiannual, and daily pay-period bracket schedules were not transcribed -- NJ-WT publishes them, but they were left out of scope to limit transcription risk on this pass. A caller using payFrequency \"quarterly\", \"semiannual\", or \"daily\" gets a clear thrown error (see bracketPerPeriodRateTable), not a silently wrong number.",
    "Supplemental wages paid on a SEPARATE cheque from regular wages (NJ-WT: \"withhold from the supplemental wages without any exemption allowances\") are not modeled -- this engine computes one paycheck at a time and cannot detect that a given cheque is supplemental-only. The same class of gap already disclosed for Kentucky.",
    "Newark's employer payroll tax (1% of payroll expense over $2,500/quarter) is a real NJ-specific tax but is employer-side and expense-based, not an employee withholding -- out of scope for this engine by the same convention as every other employer-only tax already excluded.",
    "Reciprocity with Pennsylvania is modeled (see `reciprocity` above) but was not freshly re-verified against a 2026-dated primary source this session."
